module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.executed_conjunct_discriminates_nothing

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data executed_conjunct_discriminates_nothing: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "executed_conjunct_discriminates_nothing" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**a conjunct that executes, is reached, is gated on, and still discriminates nothing** (a predicate wired into a live check runs on every call, sits inside a gate that really blocks, and yet deletes cleanly: remove it and every witness stays green, because no fixture ever constructs the population that would make it false. ",

    "**It is invisible precisely BECAUSE reachability is satisfied.** The usual signature of an unenforced mechanism -- nothing calls it -- is absent, so every reachability-based tell reports health, and review reads the conjunct as a wall because it genuinely is evaluated. ",

    "Executed and enforcing are different properties, and no amount of coverage over the calling path distinguishes them. ",

    "**It is bounded against three neighbours and none of their recognition rules will find it.** `reachability_read_as_occupancy` asks whether to DELETE a guard that is quiet, and warns that mechanism-yes / join-yes / occupancy-zero is a healthy guard; this class is not about deletion and not about occupancy -- the conjunct here should stay, and the defect is that it was believed to be doing work it was not. ",

    "Section 6's inert-lens tell is machinery that nothing GATES on; this is gated on. ",

    "Section 4b's decoration case is a check whose RED cannot be authored ANYWHERE; this RED can be authored -- it simply never was, which is the whole difference, and it is the difference between a permanent ceiling and one missing fixture. ",

    "**THE REMEDY HAS TWO HALVES AND THE SECOND IS WHAT MAKES THE FIRST SOUND.** First: for each wall, run the DELETE arm and confirm EXACTLY ONE witness reddens -- not that a witness reddens. ",

    "Second: the subject that isolates the conjunct must be chosen with care, because a red for the wrong reason is how this class survives its own test. ",

    "**A THIRD HALF, AND IT IS THE MIRROR OF THE SECOND (amended 2026-09-03, tidy-koi-619 on gunbc#10257, found by warm-seal-35): CONFIRM THE DELETE ARM ACTUALLY DELETED.** The second half guards a RED for the wrong reason; this guards a GREEN for the wrong reason, and the remedy as written above is satisfiable by a no-op. ",

    "A probe that FAILED TO MUTATE and a probe whose mutation the check TOLERATED print the identical passing value, so 'run the delete arm and read the verdict' cannot distinguish a wall that holds from a wall that was never tested. ",

    "THE PROBE MUST ASSERT THAT IT MUTATED -- count the substitutions, or diff the tree -- as a claim SEPARATE from what the check then says, and then restore and re-run to confirm the green returns, because a one-sided probe does not establish that the verdict tracks the mutation at all. ",

    "SPECIMEN, and it is worth recording because both failure paths are real rather than imagined: proving the discriminating red for every_restored_stall_is_still_rostered took THREE attempts and the first two mutated nothing. ",

    "Attempt one ran the edit through `python3 -c` under DOUBLE QUOTES, so the shell consumed the escape sequences and the replacement matched no text. ",

    "Attempt two chose an anchor that matched TWICE -- the check's own pin list had just been added to the same module as the roster and repeated the same member spellings, which is a general hazard: ANY CHECK THAT ENUMERATES ROSTER MEMBERS CREATES A SECOND POPULATION WITH THE SAME SPELLINGS, so every later sweep over that module must distinguish them. ",

    "Both attempts printed the passing value and would have been read as the wall holding. ",

    "Only the third, anchored on roster-only context, dropped the row and produced the red, with the green returning after restore. ",

    "THE CATCH WAS INCIDENTAL, WHICH IS THE ARGUMENT FOR WRITING IT DOWN: the no-ops were noticed only because the edit script happened to carry an occurrence-count assertion written for an unrelated reason. ",

    "Nothing in the remedy required it. ",

    "**A FOURTH HALF, WHICH MOVES THE ROW FROM PROBE DESIGN TO READ DESIGN (2026-09-05, vivid-ibex-751, gunbc#10345): THE VERIFICATION MUTATED NOTHING, SO THERE WAS NO MUTATION TO CONFIRM.** The third half tells an author to assert that their delete arm actually deleted, and it is scoped to a probe the author CONSTRUCTS. A read-only verification has no such arm: the artifact is not modified, nothing can fail to apply, and the third half's question -- did my edit land -- has no referent. The class survives the move intact because the invalid state does not depend on there being an edit at all: **TWO HYPOTHESES, ONE OUTPUT SHAPE, AND A REGION READ THAT IS BYTE-IDENTICAL UNDER BOTH.** ",

    "**SPECIMEN OF THE READ FORM.** The claim under test was that a generated projection renders each row's FIRST receipt string. The check run was a grep for the row's bullet, confirming it BEGAN with `receipts[0]`. It did, and the claim was false: the projection concatenates ALL receipts into one bullet. A prefix match is satisfied identically by first-receipt-only and by all-receipts-concatenated, because a concatenation STARTS WITH ITS FIRST ELEMENT -- so the region inspected could not differ between the hypothesis and its negation, and the check could not have come out any other way under either. The tail was the only discriminating region and it was never read. The disconfirming bytes were present in the same file, one line further along. ",

    "**THE RECOGNITION RULE FOR THE READ FORM IS A QUESTION ABOUT THE REGION, NOT ABOUT THE PREDICATE: NAME THE BYTES THAT WOULD DIFFER IF THE CLAIM WERE FALSE, AND CHECK THAT YOUR READ COVERS THEM.** `Did I verify it` is the wrong question and it is why this passes review: the verification is real, it executes, it reads the true artifact, and it is honest. The failure is that the WINDOW was chosen where the two hypotheses agree. A structural over-approximation of the window -- read the whole record, diff the whole file -- is the cheap discharge and is usually correct; where the window must be narrow, the narrowing must be justified by naming what distinguishes it, in the same way the second half of this row demands a red be shown to fail for the intended reason. **THE TELL IS THAT THE READER CANNOT STATE WHAT THEIR CHECK WOULD PRINT IF THE CLAIM WERE FALSE**, which is the same tell this ledger records for a change detector, arriving here with no literal and no test to inspect. ",

    "**SPECIMEN, with both halves executed** (gunbc#9838, `gunbc.self_host_compile_phase_frontier`): `census_population_is_duplicate_free` was added as a conjunct of `receipt_population_coherent`, evaluated on every coherence check and reachable from the live path; deleting it left the whole witness module green. ",

    "The fixture that isolates it is a receipt whose `refused_files` REPEATS A PATH -- enrolled as `a_receipt_whose_refused_population_repeats_a_path_is_refused_by_coherence` in `test.claim.self_host_compile_phase_frontier_witness`, with `the_same_receipt_without_the_repeat_is_coherent` as its positive control. ",

    "The subject that looks equally good and is not: a repeated ERROR DIAGNOSTIC IDENTITY also reddens the module, but it breaks a count invariant one line over rather than this conjunct, so it would have scored the DEAD conjunct as LIVE and closed the investigation with the wall still inert. ",

    "**RUNG: mechanically preventable, and the honest ceiling is the same rung rather than higher.** The unenforcing conjunct stays writable; what exists is an executed falsifier per wall, not a construction that forbids authoring one. ",

    "The next-rung trigger is a CAPABILITY and not an artifact: a mechanism that derives, from the check itself, the population its removal would change -- so that a conjunct with an empty such population fails to compile rather than waiting for an author to think of the delete arm. ",

    "Enumerating delete arms by hand does not retire it; it only executes this row's recognition rule once per wall. ",

    "**Its near twin is `instrument_output_read_as_subject_content`, and they meet from opposite sides**: there a report is complete for the REPORTER and read as complete for the SUBJECT; here a conjunct is genuinely executed and read as genuinely discriminating. ",

    "Both are the shape where the health signal the reader actually checks -- completeness there, execution here -- is fully satisfied while the property they believe it establishes does not hold. ",

    "**Neither is found by checking harder along the axis that already reads green.** **SECOND SPECIMEN, 2026-09-02, the same shape one layer down and found by a different tell.** `v1.stage0.required_regen_host` `admit_stage_execution_from_model` built ONE identity list from the stage plan and passed it as BOTH the `planned` and the `executed` field of `RegenStageExecutionObservation`, so `v2.workflow.regen_convergence_transaction` `regen_identity_population_eq` evaluated x == x.clone() on every install of the self-host convergence transaction. ",

    "The conjunct ran, the install boundary really blocked, and `StagePlannedExecutedMismatch` stayed authorable in `v2.test.claim.regen_convergence_transaction_witness_test` while being unreachable from the real acceptance path -- the exact split section 4b's authorable-RED rule exists to catch. ",

    "**THE DELETE ARM IS NOT WHAT FOUND IT; THE PRODUCER COUNT IS**, and that is this specimen's addition to the row: reading the two sides of one population equality back to their PRODUCERS and finding a single producer is cheaper than removing the conjunct and re-running, and it needs no experiment -- any equality whose two arguments trace to one value is this class already. ",

    "**THE REPAIR IS A SECOND PRODUCER, NEVER A SECOND READ OF THE FIRST**: a digest delta over the journalled generated roster, taken before the copy loop and again after the build, carried in its own Rust newtype `ObservedEffectPopulation` with no conversion from the plan, so a later refactor cannot re-collapse the two sides without deleting a type. ",

    "Its discriminating red `stage_execution_joins_the_plan_to_independently_observed_effects` carries TWO arms because one-directional identity checking is how the loss survived: an effect on a path OUTSIDE the plan, which was green before because `allowed_after` blanket-permits every already-dirty stage0 path for the rest of the transaction; and a planned surface the stage left byte-identical, which did refuse before but as `InstalledDigestMismatch` -- a CONTENT verdict standing in for a POPULATION one, so the arm asserts the cause and not that it refused.)",

    "**WIDENED 2026-09-05 PAST PREDICATES, AND THE NAME NO LONGER BOUNDS THE CLASS.** Both specimens above are predicates in gates -- a conjunct, and an `x == x.clone()` population equality -- and two lanes on 2026-09-05 (jolly-badger-374 on gunbc#10545, quick-heron-85 on the NS-N cut) independently hit the same defect in artifacts that are not predicates at all, each convinced they had found a novel class, neither having read this roster. Nothing about the class requires the artifact to be evaluated: what is common is that an artifact is BELIEVED to provide a property and is counterfactually independent of it. ",

    "**THE THREE FORMS NOW RECORDED, and the third is the one nobody looks for.** (i) A PREDICATE, above. (ii) EVIDENCE CITED IN AN ARGUMENT: quick-heron-85's `fxprobe` two-owner fixture, offered as proof that `v1.compiler.infer_sigs.containment_admits_owner` discriminates -- both binaries, chain check present and replaced by literal `true`, emitted `compiled: 8 files emitted, 0 diagnostics` and bound the identical `crate::app_api::f`. The decoy was admitted by neither, so the fixture had zero discriminating power IN EITHER DIRECTION while being cited as evidence in both. (iii) PRODUCTION CODE THAT COMPENSATES FOR NOTHING: a recursion in `realize_module` -- pre-existing, over `resolved.resolved_imports`, and REPOINTED by the lane's change onto `reference_provider_module_paths` -- believed by the author to ensure a containment-admissible owner is realized before its consumer regardless of file discovery order. Removed, with the delete arm verified to this row's own hardening standard -- zero occurrences of the symbol in the probe binary against one in the control, differing md5s, regen drift installed before the build -- every observable was byte-identical on BOTH orderings: 1065 blocking, 3206 advisory, 1061 distinct diagnostics. It also does not cause the stack overflow it was suspected of; the no-recursion binary aborts on the three-root corpus exactly as HEAD does, exit 134. FORM (iii) IS THE ONE NOBODY LOOKS FOR BECAUSE IT HAS NO SYNTACTIC SURFACE: a predicate announces itself as a claim by being a boolean in a gate and a citation announces itself by being a citation, but production code announces nothing, so the only way in is to ask what property you would name if someone asked why the code is there -- which is the belief test below, and the only one of the three tells that cannot be automated today. ",

    "**THE MEMBERSHIP TEST IS A QUESTION ABOUT BELIEF, NOT ABOUT SHAPE: does anyone believe this artifact provides a property?** If yes, this class, whether the artifact is a check, a citation, or ordinary production code. If no -- a helper nobody holds a belief about -- that is plain section 2 redundancy and a different question, which this roster does not currently carry a row for. Shape is what a reader's instinct tracks and it is the wrong axis; a conjunct wears its claim in its syntax and production code wears it in its intent, and the class is the GAP between what an artifact is believed to do and what it does. ",

    "**THE AUTHOR'S OWN EXPERIMENT DESIGN IS THE SHARPEST TELL, sharper than either receipt.** quick-heron-85 argued form (iii) was claimless and therefore a different class whose remedy was deletion. But the experiment swept the ORDERING, on both binaries -- and there is no reason to sweep a variable unless something is claimed about it. Asked directly, the answer was yes: the property was stated on the record hours earlier, that removing the recursion without first seeding the pool from the graph 'WOULD ARM THE DEFECT THIS EXPERIMENT JUST FAILED TO FIND'. So the belief was load-bearing enough to dictate the method and invisible enough that the author denied it existed one message later. AND THE BELIEF WAS NEVER AUTHORED, WHICH IS THE WORSE AND LESS VISIBLE CASE (corrected by quick-heron-85 against this row's first draft, which had the recursion added FOR the property): the recursion PREDATED the belief, and the ordering property was attributed to it afterwards as the readiest explanation for a negative result -- then hardened into a stated property that dictated the experimental design and nearly dictated the repair order. Nobody built a false claim; a claim ACCRETED onto existing code. So the class does not require anyone to have constructed the artifact for the property, and looking only for mistaken constructions will miss the accreted ones. WHEN YOU CANNOT TELL WHETHER AN ARTIFACT CARRIES A CLAIM, READ THE EXPERIMENT YOU DESIGNED TO TEST IT: the variables you chose to vary are the claim. ",

    "**THE REMEDY IS NOT `DELETE`, AND STOPPING AT DELETE IS THE ABSORBING MOVE** -- it removes the artifact AND the signal that the property was ever in question. Identical observables after removal are equally consistent with three worlds: something else holds the property, nothing ever threatened it, or it is now unprotected in a way no current fixture reaches. The single remedy covering all three forms is DELETE, THEN DETERMINE WHETHER THE PROPERTY THE ARTIFACT WAS BELIEVED TO PROVIDE IS HELD BY ANYTHING, with three terminals: author the missing fixture so a check can discriminate; establish which of the three worlds you are in; or ESTABLISH THE PROPERTY BY CONSTRUCTION so the question cannot recur -- which is the section 4b climb rather than a repair, and the only terminal that ends the class for that instance. Form (iii) took the third: the graph-seeding repair makes the pool order-independent by construction and moots which world it was in. ",

    "**WHEN A CLASS WIDENS PAST ITS NAME, THE REPAIR IS AN INBOUND POINTER FROM WHERE SEARCHERS ARRIVE, NOT A RENAME OF WHERE THE CONTENT LIVES.** This row's identity is carried by the roster, this row, the projection, sibling rows citing it by name in their bounding prose, a witness test, and the generated seed `src/v1/stage0/src/required_regen_host.rs`. THE POPULATION IS NAMED BY ITS PRODUCER RATHER THAN TRANSCRIBED, because a reference census is live and a copied count rots without either end being touched: run `git grep -l executed_conjunct_discriminates_nothing` to re-derive it. Renaming to fix DISCOVERABILITY would drag a seed regeneration onto the carrier with the worst merge contention in the repository, and would move a name that six rows cite in PROSE with no mechanical check that the prose followed. So the cost of moving a name scales with how well-connected a row is, and the best-connected rows are exactly the ones most worth finding. Pointers were instead added FROM `positional_citation`, `unlanded_citation_indistinguishable_at_the_citing_end` and `stable_citation_mutable_referent`, which is where a reader carrying form (ii) actually lands. ",

    "**RUNG, CORRECTED 2026-09-05 AFTER REVIEW FOUND THIS ROW INFLATING ITS OWN: THE AGGREGATE IS THE MINIMUM ACROSS THE THREE FORMS, AND THAT MINIMUM IS BELOW THE LADDER.** An earlier revision of this receipt said rung and ceiling were UNCHANGED by the widening -- mechanically preventable -- and that was rung inflation authored in the same breath as the widening that invalidated it. DESIGN section 4b(1) requires the reported rung to equal the rung established by EXECUTED EVIDENCE, at the minimum across a class's in-scope paths, and the receipt four entries below this one states in its own words that after this filing NOTHING is harder to do for any of the three forms. A row cannot claim a preventive rung and admit no mechanism exists; the admission is the measurement. ",

    "**PER FORM, so the aggregate is derivable rather than asserted.** (i) A PREDICATE IN A GATE: no enrolled mechanism refuses a conjunct that discriminates nothing. What the row carries is a METHOD -- delete the conjunct and rerun -- which an author must choose to apply, and an unapplied method is not a wall. (ii) EVIDENCE CITED IN AN ARGUMENT: nothing reads a fixture for discriminating power; the two-binary control that exposed the specimen was hand-built for that one question. (iii) PRODUCTION CODE COMPENSATING FOR NOTHING: no syntactic surface, so nothing can even be scanned for it, which the widening receipt above already states. All three sit BELOW THE LADDER -- not mitigatable, because there is no typed, located or countable diagnostic at any boundary for any of them -- and the aggregate is therefore below the ladder too. ",

    "**CEILING AND TRIGGER ARE GENUINELY UNCHANGED, and that half of the withdrawn sentence survives.** The ceiling stays MECHANICALLY PREVENTABLE, because the next-rung trigger is a capability and not a wall: a mechanism that derives, FROM AN ARTIFACT ITSELF, the population its removal would change, so an artifact with an empty such population fails to compile. Widening the class does not advance that trigger; it ENLARGES THE POPULATION the trigger must serve, which is a reason to state the widening rather than to leave the forms unfiled. What the correction changes is the CURRENT rung, which was reported above its evidence, and nothing about where the class can reach. ",

    "**SECOND-LAYER SPECIMEN, 2026-09-05, THE SAME COLLAPSE IN AN UNRELATED SUBSTRATE -- OUR OWN CI (found by jolly-dove, mechanism verified in the type declarations rather than from the log narrative).** `gunbc.heal_revalidation` declares `HealOutcome` with three arms -- `HealNoChange`, `HealProduced`, `HealAuthorCommitRequired` -- beside `PriorRunDisposition`'s `SupersededByHealedHead { prior_head, healed_head }`. The heal job emits the typed outcome and then exits 1, and THE EXIT 1 IS CORRECT: it refuses to let a pre-heal head stand as green. But a genuine red, a drift that was healed and needs revalidation, and an author-commit-required heal that cannot be pushed all reach every downstream reader as one value, `conclusion=failure`. The job knows which it is and says so in typed form in the log; the distinction dies at the run conclusion, which is where readers actually look. ",

    "**WHY THAT SPECIMEN IS WORTH MORE THAN A SECOND COMPILER ONE, and why it sharpens rather than merely corroborates.** A collapse shown only inside one fold of one compiler invites the reading that it is a quirk of that fold; the same shape in the build reporting of the same repository, neither case derived from the other, closes that off before it is asked. And CI's case carries an aggravating feature the compiler case lacks: THERE IS NO DEFECT AT THE PRODUCER AT ALL. The exit 1 is right, the typed outcome is right, the log is right. So this is the cleanest available statement that the class is CONSUMER-SIDE -- a producer can be flawless and the distinction still dies at the boundary where it is read -- which is also why a carrier's own header asserting that its arms are 'never collapsed' is not evidence about the property a consumer actually has. ",

    "**THIS APPEND IS A RECORD AND NOT A REPAIR, STATED PLAINLY BECAUSE `a_written_row_is_not_a_firing_mechanism` DEMANDS IT OF ANY FILING.** Its test is: after filing, what is now HARDER to do than it was before? For these three forms the honest answer is NOTHING. An author can still cite a fixture that discriminates nothing, still ship a compensating branch whose removal changes no observable, still attribute a property to code that never provided it. So the class stands UNREMEDIED at its existing rung, and this widening must not be read as coverage -- a filed class gets cited as handled, which converts an open deficit into a closed-looking one and is a section 4b(1) rung wearing a 4b(2) costume. What the widening buys is RECOGNITION SURFACE: three forms instead of one, a membership test that does not depend on the artifact's shape, and a remedy with three terminals. The friction artefact this class needs remains unbuilt and unclaimed. ",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
